{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>The desire of a man</b> — is to do his kindness, that is, he always desires to do kindness to one worthy of it. Or תאות is from נאוה קדש." "<b>And a poor man is better than a lying man</b> — who says he will do kindness but is lying — the poor man is better than him, like: 'a man boasting of a false gift.'"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The phrase נאוה קדש is quoted in Hebrew script exactly as in the source; Ibn Ezra is citing an occurrence of the root תאה in construct form as a lexical parallel.", 1 "The comparison 'like: a man boasting...' alludes to Proverbs 25:14, rendered here as a gloss on the parallel rather than as a full citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:42.474362646Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}